84→                </div>\n   285→\n   286→                <div class=\"item\">\n   287→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   288→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/KangarooKi/Ultracode\" target=\"_blank\">Ultracode</a>\n   289→                    </div>\n   290→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   291→                        A local AI-assisted coding CLI inspired by Claude Code. Runs agentic coding workflows in your workspace with OpenAI-compatible models, function-calling tools, task planning, memory, and permissions.\n   292→                    </div>\n   293→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   294→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   295→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-31</span>\n   296→                    </div>\n   297→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Terminal-first coding agent for developers\"</div>\n   298→                </div>\n   299→\n   300→                <div class=\"item\">\n   301→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   302→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/tathagat22/plumb-mcp\" target=\"_blank\">plumb-mcp</a>\n   303→                    </div>\n   304→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   305→                        A local Figma MCP server with no REST rate limits, no metered tool-call quotas, and a verification loop. A drop-in alternative to Figma's Dev Mode MCP.\n   306→                    </div>\n   307→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   308→                        <span class=\"category\">MCP server</span>\n   309→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-23</span>\n   310→                    </div>\n   311→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Works on every plan including Free\"</div>\n   312→                </div>\n   313→\n   314→                <div class=\"item\">\n   315→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   316→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/ntd4996/agentpet\" target=\"_blank\">agentpet</a>\n   317→                    </div>\n   318→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   319→                        A native macOS menu bar app with a desktop pet that monitors your AI coding agents (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI) in real time. Provides visual feedback and monitoring for terminal-based AI coding workflows.\n   320→                    </div>\n   321→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   322→                        <span class=\"category\">Desktop monitoring</span>\n   323→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-31</span>\n   324→                    </div>\n   325→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"A desktop pet that monitors your AI coding agents in real time\"</div>\n   326→                </div>\n   327→\n   328→                <div class=\"item\">\n   329→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   330→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/XWJDream/MimoAgent\" target=\"_blank\">MimoAgent</a>\n   331→                    </div>\n   332→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   333→                        AI-powered coding assistant desktop app based on Xiaomi MiMo. Supports code generation, debugging, refactoring, project analysis, MCP tools, and TTS.\n   334→                    </div>\n   335→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   336→                        <span class=\"category\">Desktop AI</span>\n   337→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-30</span>\n   338→                    </div>\n   339→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Comprehensive AI coding assistance in a desktop app\"</div>\n   340→                </div>\n   341→\n   342→                <div class=\"item\">\n   343→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   344→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Daaaaave/agentic-workspace-core\" target=\"_blank\">agentic-workspace-core</a>\n   345→                    </div>\n   346→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   347→                        A portable repository-native foundation for agent memory, skills, handoffs, and knowledge workflows. Provides project-long memory and workspace management across AI coding sessions.\n   348→                    </div>\n   349→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   350→                        <span class=\"category\">Memory framework</span>\n   351→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-23</span>\n   352→                    </div>\n   353→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Knowledge workflows for AI agents\"</div>\n   354→                </div>\n   355→\n   356→                <div class=\"item\">\n   357→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   358→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/68110923/rx-gui\" target=\"_blank\">rx-gui (Reasonix)</a>\n   359→                    </div>\n   360→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   361→                        JetBrains IDE AI Coding Assistant plugin featuring DeepSeek AI integration. Supports streaming conversations, Markdown rendering, code diff review, and cost tracking.\n   362→                    </div>\n   363→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   364→                        <span class=\"category\">JetBrains plugin</span>\n   365→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-24</span>\n   366→                    </div>\n   367→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"JetBrains IDE AI Coding Assistant with DeepSeek AI\"</div>\n   368→                </div>\n   369→\n   370→                <div class=\"item\">\n   371→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   372→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/vikingmute/review-forge\" target=\"_blank\">review-forge</a>\n   373→                    </div>\n   374→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   375→                        An Agent Skill for structured, auditable code review workflows. Provides workflow-specific code review capabilities for AI coding agents.\n   376→                    </div>\n   377→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   378→                        <span class=\"category\">Code review</span>\n   379→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-29</span>\n   380→                    </div>\n   381→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Structured, auditable code review workflows\"</div>\n   382→                </div>\n   383→\n   384→                <div class=\"item\">\n   385→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   386→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/sigmashakeinc/vscode\" target=\"_blank\">SigmaShake SSG</a>\n   387→                    </div>\n   388→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   389→                        VS Code extension for AI governance, guardrails, audit, and .rules language support. Provides oversight and policy enforcement for Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Gemini, and MCP assistants.\n   390→                    </div>\n   391→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   392→                        <span class=\"category\">VS Code extension</span>\n   393→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-25</span>\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"AI governance, guardrails, audit & .rules language support\"</div>\n   396→                </div>\n   397→\n   398→                <div class=\"item\">\n   399→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   400→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/m-aboud/openclaw-devops-copilot\" target=\"_blank\">openclaw-devops-copilot</a>\n   401→                    </div>\n   402→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   403→                        DevOps Copilot: an AI-powered assistant for DevOps workflows, infrastructure as code generation, and SRE tasks. Helps orchestrate complex development operations workflows.\n   404→                    </div>\n   405→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   406→                        <span class=\"category\">DevOps agent</span>\n   407→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-06-01</span>\n   408→                    </div>\n   409→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"AI-powered assistant for DevOps workflows\"</div>\n   410→                </div>\n   411→\n   412→                <div class=\"item\">\n   413→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   414→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/MagWizD/alethia-clients\" target=\"_blank\">alethia-clients</a>\n   415→                    </div>\n   416→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   417→                        VSCode extension and JetBrains plugin for Aletheia that passively detects and attributes AI-generated code contributions by serializing flagged metadata as git notes on each commit.\n   418→                    </div>\n   419→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   420→                        <span class=\"category\">AI attribution</span>\n   421→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-25</span>\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Passively detects and attributes AI-generated code contributions\"</div>\n   424→                </div>\n   425→\n   426→                <div class=\"item\">\n   427→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   428→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/uuhan/ai.nvim\" target=\"_blank\">ai.nvim</a>\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   431→                        A Neovim plugin for AI agent integration. Provides AI capabilities directly within the Neovim editor environment.\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   434→                        <span class=\"category\">Neovim plugin</span>\n   435→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-06-04</span>\n   436→                    </div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Your final AI plugin for Neovim\"</div>\n   438→                </div>\n   439→\n   440→                <div class=\"item\">\n   441→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   442→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/kzoldyk/baton\" target=\"_blank\">baton</a>\n   443→                    </div>\n   444→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   445→                        Desktop app for cross-agent AI handoffs. Pass project context, git diffs, and task states seamlessly between Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and other AI coding agents.\n   446→                    </div>\n   447→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   448→                        <span class=\"category\">Agent orchestration</span>\n   449→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-05-23</span>\n   450→                    </div>\n   451→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"Desktop app for cross-agent AI handoffs\"</div>\n   452→                </div>\n   453→\n   454→                <div class=\"item\">\n   455→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   456→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/kavishsathia/inline\" target=\"_blank\">inline</a>\n   457→                    </div>\n   458→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   459→                        Inline comments from an AI coding agent to your IDE. Designed for developers who prefer IDE integration over terminal-based AI coding agents or desktop apps.\n   460→                    </div>\n   461→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   462→                        <span class=\"category\">IDE integration</span>\n   463→                        <span>GitHub</span> · <span>2026-06-02</span>\n   464→                    </div>\n   465→                    <div class=\"quote\">\"For those who can't read off a terminal\"</div>\n   466→                </div>\n   467→            </section>\n   468→\n   469→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   470→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   471→                <h2>Whitelist Updates <span class=\"section-count\">11</span></h2>\n   472→\n   473→                <div class=\"item\">\n   474→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   475→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.163\" target=\"_blank\">\n   476→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.163</span> Enterprise Version Management\n   477→                        </a>\n   478→                    </div>\n   479→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   480→                        Added version management controls for enterprise deployments, enhanced plugin management with /plugin list command supporting filters, improved /btw with clipboard copy shortcut, and enhanced hooks capabilities.\n   481→                    </div>\n   482→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   483→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   484→                        <span>2026-06-04</span>\n   485→                    </div>\n   486→                </div>\n   487→\n   488→                <div class=\"item\">\n   489→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   490→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.162\" target=\"_blank\">\n   491→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.162</span> Enhanced Agent CLI\n   492→                        </a>\n   493→                    </div>\n   494→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   495→                        Enhanced claude agents --json with waitingFor field showing session blockers, improved tool specification for Grep/Glob on native builds, added /effort persistence confirmation, and enhanced slash command autocomplete behavior.\n   496→                    </div>\n   497→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   498→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   499→                        <span>2026-06-03</span>\n   500→                    </div>\n   501→                </div>\n   502→\n   503→                <div class=\"item\">\n   504→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   505→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.161\" target=\"_blank\">\n   506→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.161</span> OpenTelemetry Integration\n   507→                        </a>\n   508→                    </div>\n   509→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   510→                        OpenTelemetry integration with custom label support via OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES, improved claude agents UI with progress indicators, enhanced /mcp connector management, and improved parallel tool call error handling.\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   513→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   514→                        <span>2026-06-02</span>\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                </div>\n   517→\n   518→                <div class=\"item\">\n   519→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   520→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.160\" target=\"_blank\">\n   521→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.160</span> Safety Prompts\n   522→                        </a>\n   523→                    </div>\n   524→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   525→                        Added safety prompts before writing to shell startup files and git config, enhanced acceptEdits mode to prompt before build-tool config writes, improved Edit tool behavior after grep operations.\n   526→                    </div>\n   527→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   528→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   529→                        <span>2026-06-02</span>\n   530→                    </div>\n   531→                </div>\n   532→\n   533→                <div class=\"item\">\n   534→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   535→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.158\" target=\"_blank\">\n   536→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.158</span> Auto Mode Expansion\n   537→                        </a>\n   538→                    </div>\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   540→                        Extended Auto mode support to Bedrock, Vertex, and Foundry platforms for Opus 4.7 and 4.8 models via CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_AUTO_MODE=1 environment variable.\n   541→                    </div>\n   542→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   543→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   544→                        <span>2026-05-30</span>\n   545→                    </div>\n   546→                </div>\n   547→\n   548→                <div class=\"item\">\n   549→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   550→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.157\" target=\"_blank\">\n   551→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.157</span> Automatic Plugin Loading\n   552→                        </a>\n   553→                    </div>\n   554→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   555→                        Automatic plugin loading from .claude/skills directories, added claude plugin init scaffolding command, enhanced plugin autocomplete, improved claude agents with settings.json support, and enhanced EnterWorktree switching capabilities.\n   556→                    </div>\n   557→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   558→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   559→                        <span>2026-05-29</span>\n   560→                    </div>\n   561→                </div>\n   562→\n   563→                <div class=\"item\">\n   564→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   565→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.156\" target=\"_blank\">\n   566→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.156</span> Critical Opus Fix\n   567→                        </a>\n   568→                    </div>\n   569→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   570→                        Fixed critical issue with Opus 4.8 where thinking blocks were being modified, causing API errors.\n   571→                    </div>\n   572→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   573→                        <span class=\"category\">bugfix</span>\n   574→                        <span>2026-05-29</span>\n   575→                    </div>\n   576→                </div>\n   577→\n   578→                <div class=\"item\">\n   579→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   580→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.154\" target=\"_blank\">\n   581→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.154</span> Opus 4.8 Launch\n   582→                        </a>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   585→                        Introduced Opus 4.8 with high-effort default (/effort xhigh), launched dynamic workflows orchestrating tens to hundreds of background agents, reduced Fast mode cost to 2x standard rate for 2.5x speed.\n   586→                    </div>\n   587→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   588→                        <span class=\"category\">release</span>\n   589→                        <span>2026-05-28</span>\n   590→                    </div>\n   591→                </div>\n   592→\n   593→                <div class=\"item\">\n   594→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   595→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.153\" target=\"_blank\">\n   596→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.153</span> Plugin Sources & Diagnostics\n   597→                        </a>\n   598→                    </div>\n   599→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   600→                        Added skipLfs option for GitHub/git plugin sources, added npm global install auto-update notice with /doctor diagnostics, enhanced status line commands with terminal size environment variables.\n   601→                    </div>\n   602→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   603→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   604→                        <span>2026-05-28</span>\n   605→                    </div>\n   606→                </div>\n   607→\n   608→                <div class=\"item\">\n   609→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   610→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.152\" target=\"_blank\">\n   611→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.152</span> Enhanced Code Review\n   612→                        </a>\n   613→                    </div>\n   614→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   615→                        Enhanced /code-review --fix to apply findings and renamed /simplify to /code-review, added disallowed-tools frontmatter for skills/slash commands, added /reload-skills command.\n   616→                    </div>\n   617→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   618→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   619→                        <span>2026-05-27</span>\n   620→                    </div>\n   621→                </div>\n   622→\n   623→                <div class=\"item\">\n   624→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   625→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.149\" target=\"_blank\">\n   626→                            <span class=\"version-badge\">v2.1.149</span> Usage Analytics\n   627→                        </a>\n   628→                    </div>\n   629→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   630→                        Enhanced /usage with per-category breakdown (skills, subagents, plugins, MCP servers), improved /diff detail view with keyboard scrolling, added GFM task list checkbox rendering.\n   631→                    </div>\n   632→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   633→                        <span class=\"category\">feature</span>\n   634→                        <span>2026-05-22</span>\n   635→                    </div>\n   636→                </div>\n   637→            </section>\n   638→\n   639→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   640→            <section class=\"technical-insights\">\n   641→                <h2>Technical Insights <span class=\"section-count\">3</span></h2>\n   642→\n   643→                <div class=\"item\">\n   644→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   645→                        <a href=\"https://www.brethorsting.com/blog/2026/05/domain-expertise-has-always-been-the-real-moat/\" target=\"_blank\">Domain expertise has always been the real moat</a>\n   646→                    </div>\n   647→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   648→                        Discussion on how domain expertise remains critical even with AI advances. The conversation touches on how AI coding tools and LLMs change (but don't eliminate) the value of deep technical knowledge.\n   649→                    </div>\n   650→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   651→                        Aaron Brethorst · <span>2026-05-30</span>\n   652→                    </div>\n   653→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   654→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI coding</span>\n   655→                        <span class=\"topic\">domain expertise</span>\n   656→                        <span class=\"topic\">developer skills</span>\n   657→                    </div>\n   658→                </div>\n   659→\n   660→                <div class=\"item\">\n   661→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   662→                        <a href=\"https://openrouter.ai/announcements/series-b\" target=\"_blank\">OpenRouter raises $113M Series B</a>\n   663→                    </div>\n   664→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   665→                        OpenRouter, an AI model routing platform, raised $113M in Series B funding. This highlights continued investment in AI infrastructure and developer tooling for accessing multiple LLM APIs through unified interfaces.\n   666→                    </div>\n   667→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   668→                        OpenRouter Team · <span>2026-05-30</span>\n   669→                    </div>\n   670→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   671→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI infrastructure</span>\n   672→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM routing</span>\n   673→                        <span class=\"topic\">funding</span>\n   674→                    </div>\n   675→                </div>\n   676→\n   677→                <div class=\"item\">\n   678→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   679→                        <a href=\"https://claude.ai/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Claude Opus 4.8 Launch and Dynamic Workflows</a>\n   680→                    </div>\n   681→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   682→                        Anthropic released Claude Opus 4.8 with improved performance and accuracy. Introduced dynamic workflows that adapt to task complexity. Enhanced terminal interaction with better command suggestions and multi-step execution support.\n   683→                    </div>\n   684→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   685→                        Anthropic · <span>2026-05-29</span>\n   686→                    </div>\n   687→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   688→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n   689→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI coding</span>\n   690→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n   691→                        <span class=\"topic\">agentic workflows</span>\n   692→                    </div>\n   693→                </div>\n   694→            </section>\n   695→        </main>\n   696→\n   697→        <footer>\n   698→            <a href=\"#\">Archives</a> |\n   699→            <a href=\"#\">About</a> |\n   700→            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a> |\n   701→            <a href=\"#\">GitHub</a>\n   702→            <br><br>\n   703→            Generated with ❤️ for the agentic coding community\n   704→        </footer>\n   705→    </div>\n   706→</body>\n   707→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
      }
    ]
