ter, an AI model routing platform, raised $113M in Series B funding. This highlights continued investment in AI infrastructure and developer tooling for accessing multiple LLM APIs through unified interfaces.\n   757→                        </div>\n   758→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   759→                            <span class=\"source-link\">OpenRouter Team</span>\n   760→                            <span> • </span>\n   761→                            <span class=\"source-link\">Hacker News</span>\n   762→                            <span> • </span>\n   763→                            <span>2026-05-30</span>\n   764→                        </div>\n   765→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   766→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI infrastructure</span>\n   767→                            <span class=\"tag\">LLM routing</span>\n   768→                            <span class=\"tag\">funding</span>\n   769→                        </div>\n   770→                    </div>\n   771→\n   772→                    <div class=\"insight-item\">\n   773→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   774→                            <a href=\"https://claude.ai/changelog\">Claude Opus 4.8 Launch and Dynamic Workflows</a>\n   775→                        </div>\n   776→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   777→                            Anthropic released Claude Opus 4.8 with improved performance and accuracy. Introduced dynamic workflows that adapt to task complexity. Enhanced terminal interaction with better command suggestions and multi-step execution support.\n   778→                        </div>\n   779→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   780→                            <span class=\"source-link\">Anthropic / Claude Team</span>\n   781→                            <span> • </span>\n   782→                            <span class=\"source-link\">TechMedia</span>\n   783→        